  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through next Tuesday) \nIssued at 1129 AM CDT Tue Oct 13 2026\n\nOnce we get through Thursday, a dry front is going to deliver autumn \nback to the mid-state. Models are very consistent bringing this \nfront through here on Friday and providing a break in this heat. The \nweekend looks dry and cool -- maybe 10 degree below seasonal norms.\n\nYep, I said \"a break\" in the heat. We may not be done with it yet. \nThe cooler temperatures want to stay, but models are relatively \nconsistent bringing yet another upper ridge into the southeast US \nnext week and providing above normal temperatures once again. \nObviously, that's a week out, but fall doesn't look like it's here \nto stay and other than the rain in the north tomorrow, continued dry \nconditions will be with us until *at least* this time next week.",
